@clawsweeper re-review

Please review updated head `48e86662660ee3b8270fb1c4fe2309cb3bcbcb8b`. The previous request completed. This head integrates upstream tip `e76ebe68919c7a71881e7235c70f39ddafc4be3f`, resolves all three conflicts, and adds the current-descriptor title repair with its red-to-green regression. All 110 focused steering/mailbox tests, seven UI metadata tests and three cold-load browser tests pass, along with core/UI types and scoped typed lint/format. GitHub reports the branch mergeable; hosted CI remains pending.

The PR body is current. The [exceptional queued-authority traces](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/177698#issuecomment-6292768497) retain their actual e44 revision and fault-injection qualifications: all 44 source pins are unchanged at this head, but this is source-qualified reuse, not a new native execution of the merged binary. The original CI ordering remains unestablished. Security-owner acceptance, the accepted-human optional reply decision and the stated remaining proof limits are still explicit.

@clawsweeper re-review

Current head: `5d74c50003122fe40da34b36eac16e838e5857d3`. The reported conflict is resolved by integrating upstream `1429fd5487b`; the single manual resolution preserves the reorganized error-handling cases and claim-change error assertion. Independent resolution review, 30 affected Bun tests, focused lint/format, and the widget Chromium test pass. Upstream #178645 supplies deterministic touch-event timestamps, with all existing scrolling assertions retained.

The body is updated. The earlier Linux maintenance failure remains unexplained; a local pass is not claimed as its repair. Earlier native/authority captures remain revision-qualified. Security-owner and session-owner decisions remain explicitly open. No Gateway restart or deployment was performed.
